[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4956417607","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121318#issuecomment-4956417607","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121318","id":4956417607,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ2zuRw","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-13T09:23:14Z","updated_at":"2026-07-13T09:51:27Z","body":"> Unfortunately, this PR will not be able to recover manual triangles saved with 4.7 while the regression was active.\r\n\r\nWhat does this mean specifically? Does it mean that triangles aren't stored correctly into `.tres` in 4.7 to begin with?\r\n\r\nSince the property itself wasn't removed in `https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110369`, I assume the triangles are still retained in the `.tres` file if _set_triangles() is called in 4.7. So if you open version 4.6 in 4.7 and then save it, the triangles you created manually in 4.6 will be lost, but aren't the triangles you created manually in 4.7 stored in the `.tres`?\r\n\r\nAlthough the PR #120710 was not correct in terms of code quality (it contained too many duplicates and AI generated), but I assume the point raised about the incorrect order of `add_triangle()` was valid.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4956417607/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4956892859","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121318#issuecomment-4956892859","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121318","id":4956892859,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ3Quuw","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-13T10:17:03Z","updated_at":"2026-07-13T10:39:06Z","body":"> So if you open version 4.6 in 4.7 and then save it, the triangles you created manually in 4.6 will be lost...\r\n\r\nNot lost at that point, just erroneously saved above `blend_point_i/*`, when it should be below.\r\n\r\n```\r\n [sub_resource type=\"AnimationNodeBlendSpace2D\" id=\"AnimationNodeBlendSpace2D_gllyd\"]\r\n auto_triangles = false\r\n+triangles = PackedInt32Array(0, 1, 3, 0, 2, 3)\r\n blend_point_0/node = SubResource(\"AnimationNodeBlendSpace1D_nebll\")\r\n blend_point_0/pos = Vector2(-0.5, 0.2)\r\n+blend_point_0/name = &\"0\"\r\n blend_point_1/node = SubResource(\"AnimationNodeBlendSpace1D_jx8lu\")\r\n blend_point_1/pos = Vector2(-0.1, 0.8)\r\n+blend_point_1/name = &\"1\"\r\n blend_point_2/node = SubResource(\"AnimationNodeBlendSpace2D_nharf\")\r\n blend_point_2/pos = Vector2(-0.2, -0.6)\r\n+blend_point_2/name = &\"2\"\r\n blend_point_3/node = SubResource(\"AnimationNodeBlendSpace1D_20tj1\")\r\n blend_point_3/pos = Vector2(0.2, 0.1)\r\n-triangles = PackedInt32Array(0, 1, 3, 0, 2, 3)\r\n+blend_point_3/name = &\"3\"\r\n```\r\n4.6 to 4.7 misplaces `triangles`.\r\n4.7 to this PR wipes it, and writes it afresh in the correct place. But the old data can be recovered via version control if a .tres and not a .res was used.\r\n4.6 to this PR is safe.\r\n\r\n> Although the PR #120710 was not correct in terms of code quality (it contained too many duplicates and AI generated), but I assume the point raised about the incorrect order of `add_triangle()` was valid.\r\n\r\nYes it was, and recovering from regression-affected files would look something like their PR, I think. It's a fair bit of code that would mean changing `_set_triangles` just for catching it (and might lose safety in the process), hence my comment:\r\n\r\n> I don't think we should add code just for this slim period of time the regression was active, but if there's an opposing opinion, I can look into it.\r\n\r\nIs there a less permanent way this could be handled?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4956892859/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4957070111","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121318#issuecomment-4957070111","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121318","id":4957070111,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ3bjHw","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-13T10:39:15Z","updated_at":"2026-07-13T12:31:49Z","body":"I assume add a `#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED` block inside `_set_triangle()` and if `_set_triangle()` attempts to find missing vertices, I think you can use `deferred` or something similar to wait for the set operation from `.tres` to complete, and then call `add_triangle()` again.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4957070111/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.g